<!-- ── Constant ops note ── -->
<div class="note">
  <h3>Key observations</h3>
  <div class="note-grid">
    <div class="note-item">
      <div class="ni-lbl">Fusion + copy ops are identical across input lengths</div>
      <p>
        <code>fusion</code> (FFN+QKV proj), <code>copy</code>, <code>copy_bitcast</code>, <code>pad_maximum</code>,
        and <code>broadcast.clone</code> show <strong>exactly the same times</strong> at input=1000 and input=4096.
        The profiler captures a mixed prefill/decode step where the number of <em>new Q tokens</em> is fixed —
        only the KV attention context length changes. QKV projection and FFN scale with new tokens; attention scales with kv_len.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-item">
      <div class="ni-lbl">RPA regression narrows with more kv_tiles</div>
      <p>
        RPA ratio improves from <strong>3.77×</strong> (≈2 kv_tiles/seq) → <strong>2.06×</strong> (≈8 kv_tiles/seq),
        matching the kernel_bench result of <strong>1.72×</strong> (also 8 kv_tiles/seq).
        More kv_tiles means deeper pipeline — the DMA serialisation overhead from the has_kvproj
        race-condition fix gets amortised over more bkv iterations, hiding more latency.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-item">
      <div class="ni-lbl">Fixed per-layer overhead in mega</div>
      <p>
        <code>copy_bitcast</code> (1.34ms), <code>broadcast.clone</code> (0.83ms), and
        excess <code>pad_maximum</code> (0.83ms) together add <strong>3.0ms per forward pass</strong>
        regardless of kv_len. These are x-staging and padding overheads from the per-tile projection path
        and cannot be amortised by longer sequences.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-item">
      <div class="ni-lbl">Net accounting at input=4096</div>
      <p>
        Mega saves <strong>6.39ms</strong> in external QKV proj.
        It adds <strong>+42.98ms</strong> in RPA overhead and <strong>+3.0ms</strong> in fixed per-layer ops.
        Net: <strong>+39.59ms regression</strong> per forward pass at kv_len=4096.
        Breakeven would require kv_tiles ≫ current range.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

